workedExamples.solution_text:
Each angle of an equilateral triangle is $60^{\circ}$. The altitude forms a right triangle with hypotenuse $8\text{ cm}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2,0)--(2,3.4641)--cycle;
\draw (1.75,0)--(1.75,0.25)--(2,0.25);
\draw (0.55,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=60,radius=0.55];
\path (1,1.732) node[above left] {$8\text{ cm}$} (2,1.732) node[right] {$x$} (0.9,0.48) node {$60^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{align*}\sin60^{\circ}&=\frac{x}{8}\\\frac{\sqrt3}{2}&=\frac{x}{8}\\x&=4\sqrt3\text{ cm}\end{align*}$

